{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"justjack420","id":"592252026226999306","is_bot":0,"username":"justjack420"},"author_id":"592252026226999306","channel_id":"746939355003748354","content":"Mantle of the Swarm\nRequires Attunement\n\nWoven clover and flowers make up this cloak. Among the petals bees fly between the flowers, pollinating.\n\nWhile attuned to this cloak you can cast Infestation as a bonus action. Your spell casting modifier is Wisdom.\n\nAs a reaction to getting hit, you can have the bees swarm the aggressor stinging them. Make an attack roll, with Wisdom as modifier, if it hits deal 4d4 magical piercing damage. You may use this 3 times per day.\n\n(the bees that gather on the mantle are Fae in nature and do not die when they sting.)","created_at":"2020-08-27T00:07:14.366000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"748332764327182357","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
